# P4: GitHub README and Version Tags

## Objective
To create project documentation using README.md and understand Git version tagging.

## Work Completed
1. Updated the README.md file with project information.
2. Added the project description, features, and technologies used.
3. Documented the Git workflow.
4. Committed the README changes.
5. Created an annotated Git version tag named `v1.0`.

## Git Commands Used

```bash
git add README.md
git commit -m "Update README with portfolio documentation"
git tag -a v1.0 -m "Version 1.0"
git tag
git log --oneline --decorate
git status
```

## Result
Successfully updated project documentation and created the Git version tag `v1.0`.